{
 "_readme": "Answer-melody phrase library (2026-10-19). Each entry is one short motif that plays in the back half of bars 2 and 4: 'cells' = the 16th-note steps (8-15) it lands on, 'moves' = how many scale steps each note moves from the one before (one fewer than cells; 0 repeats a note; a 3 or 4 is the one leap and must be followed by -1). The notes themselves still come from the key and the chords, and strong beats still land on chord tones. Used only by beats stamped melody_flow 2 or higher; older beats rebuild exactly as made. To add one: copy any entry and change it.",
